! Example theatre show: a short play for the lights of "Example show.json".
!
! A show file in the USITT ASCII format, the plain text that theatre consoles such as
! ETC Eos write to hand a show to another console. This one was written by hand, to show
! what Lumenet's IMPORT key does with such a file: press IMPORT and choose this file.
! Everything after "!" on a line is a comment.

Ident 3:0
Clear All

! The patch: which console channel drives which DMX address (the channel faders of
! Lumenet). Read "1<3@100" as: channel 1 drives address 3 at 100 %. Channel 4 drives two
! blue lights at once, and channel 8 gives the right pot 80 % of its level.
Patch 1 1<3@100 2<4@100 3<5@100
Patch 1 4<6@100 4<7@100 5<8@100 5<9@100
Patch 1 6<10@100 7<1@100 8<2@80
Patch 1 9<11@100 10<12@100 11<13@100 12<14@100
Patch 1 13<17@100 14<15@100 15<16@100

! The cues. A cue lists every channel that is up in it; the others go to zero.
! Levels are in percent; FL is full.

Cue 0.5
Text Preset
Up 5
Chan 13/FL 7/20 8/20

Cue 1
Text House to half
Up 5
Down 5
Chan 13/50 7/20 8/20

! No channels at all: everything goes out, in 3 seconds.
Cue 2
Text Blackout
Down 3

Cue 3
Text Dawn
Up 10
Down 3
Chan 4/30 5/30

Cue 4
Text Morning
Up 8
Down 5
Chan 1/FL 2/FL 3/80 4/20 5/20

Cue 4.5
Text Spot on the door
Up 2
Down 2
Chan 1/FL 2/FL 3/80 4/20 5/20 6/FL

! A cue in two parts: the front comes up first, the LED bar 3 seconds later.
Cue 5
Text Kitchen
Part 1
Up 3
Chan 1/FL 2/FL 3/FL
Part 2
Up 5 3
Chan 9/50 10/25

! A storm: cue 6 follows on by itself to 6.1 two seconds after it started, and 6.1 to 6.2.
Cue 6
Text Storm
Up 1
Down 1
Followon 2
Chan 4/20 5/20 14/30

Cue 6.1
Text Lightning
Up 0
Down 0.5
Followon 0.5
Chan 4/FL 5/FL 12/FL 14/30

Cue 6.2
Text After the flash
Up 0.5
Down 2
Chan 4/20 5/20 14/40

Cue 7
Text Evening
Up 15
Down 10
Chan 7/60 8/60 9/FL 10/40 4/15 5/15

! A fade of one and a half minutes. The $$ line only one maker's consoles understand
! (an effect of the Strand LightPalette): Lumenet skips it.
Cue 8
Text Night
Up 1:30
Down 20
$$Effect 2
Chan 4/40 5/40 15/FL

Cue 9
Text Bows
Up 3
Down 3
Chan 1/FL 2/FL 3/FL 4/FL 5/FL 12/FL

! The last cue links to the first: after it the show starts again.
Cue 10
Text House up
Up 5
Down 5
Chan 13/FL
Link 0.5

! Submasters: faders of their own on the console.
Sub 1
Text Haze
Chan 14/30

Sub 2
Text Work light
Chan 1/FL 2/FL 3/FL 13/FL

! Groups: channels that belong together.
Group 1
Text Front
Chan 1/FL 2/FL 3/FL

Group 2
Text Back blue
Chan 4/FL 5/FL

Group 3
Text Pots
Chan 7/FL 8/FL

EndData
